This project is a fork of okhttp-json-mock by Mohammad Mirrajabi
(https://github.com/mirrajabi/okhttp-json-mock), which is licensed under the
Apache License, Version 2.0. It continues the original library from version 3.0.

Changes made in this fork since version 3.0:

- The library was rewritten in Kotlin and its package was renamed from
  ir.mirrajabi.okhttpjsonmock to io.github.brodriro.okhttpjsonmock.
- Mock files can be selected by HTTP method and can set the status code,
  the headers and the latency of the response.
- A mock file or folder named {id} answers any value of that path segment.
- A request without a mock is answered with a 404 instead of an exception.
- Interceptors are immutable and are configured through a builder, which can
  also make a missing mock fail and record the calls received, for tests.
- The sample application was rewritten in Kotlin.
- A provider for mock files on the classpath is included.
